WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.450
Some of these popular TV series are too scary
to watch without a companion.

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.700
Others are just terribly, horribly sad.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:07.600
Bottom line?

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.520
You should definitely phone a friend to keep
you company before you start binging any of

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:12.120
these shows.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.320
After all, misery loves company!

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:15.840
"God, I love you."

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:21.060
The X-Files still definitely has that X factor
when it comes to being scary, particularly

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:22.400
in the early seasons.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:27.940
David Duchovny and Gillian Anderson star as
FBI agents Fox Mulder and Dana Scully, who

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.440
are tasked with investigating the bureau's
unexplainable cases.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:37.460
Their investigations lead them to a long series-spanning
arc involving alien abductions and colonization,

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.680
but the real frights come from the show's
"monster of the week" episodes.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:46.100
Take, for example, the early season one episodes
"Squeeze" and "Tooms," which tell the tale

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.460
of a man who can stretch his body to squeeze
through small spaces.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.019
He makes a nest of his own bile to hibernate
and resurface every few decades to murder

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:55.720
his victims.

00:00:56.109 --> 00:00:59.660
Then there's "Home," an episode that has been
called one of the most frightening of the

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:04.180
series, and was forbidden from being replayed
on Fox when the series turned to reruns.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.680
The less you know the better, but trust us
when we say it's truly terrifying on a whole

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:09.920
buttload of levels.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:11.840
"Federal agent, I'm armed!"

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:16.480
"Stop or I'll fire!"

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.600
Netflix's The Haunting of Hill House is a
loose adaptation of the 1959 novel of the

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.460
same name by horror fiction master Shirley
Jackson.

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:31.040
It takes place in multiple time periods and
follows a set of siblings, the Crain children,

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:35.909
whose lives are forever affected by some seriously
frightening and traumatic events at a mansion

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:37.160
known as Hill House.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:42.469
TV Line recently voted the episode "The Bent-Neck
Lady", which explores the very real horrors

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:47.469
of sleep paralysis, as the Best Single Episode
of Television in the Drama category for the

00:01:47.469 --> 00:01:49.320
entirety of 2018.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:52.700
That ought to give you an idea of how powerful
the show can be.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.000
To top it all off, it sounds like Hill House
might be going the anthology route.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.760
Creator Mike Flanagan told Entertainment Weekly:

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.520
"I don't want to speculate too much about
season two…

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:06.620
What I will say, though, is that as far as
I've ever been concerned with this, the story

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.120
of the Crain family is told.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:08.940
It's done."

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:13.540
It's hard to imagine something scarier than
a television series based on the works of

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.980
horror master Stephen King.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:20.390
Hulu's Castle Rock draws on many of King's
locations, tales, and characters combined

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:25.520
into one creepy series starring André Holland
as a criminal attorney, Melanie Lynskey as

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:30.110
a real estate agent who can read minds, and
Bill Skarsgård as a Shawshank inmate who

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:32.180
claims to be from an alternate dimension.

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:37.360
With references to King's works The Green
Mile, Misery, The Shining, and many, many

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:41.800
more, Castle Rock seeks to capture a certain
signature horror that King is known for.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:46.160
It's not always jump-in-your-seat scary, but
the showrunners have lovingly adapted the

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.900
mood and feel of King's work.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:52.080
Particular acclaim has been given to the episode
"The Queen," which focuses on a character

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.200
played by the fabulous Sissy Spacek.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.360
It might be a bit more sad than scary, but
hey, watching sad things alone isn't a great

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:00.080
idea, either.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:03.720
"I feel light in the head.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:09.820
Would you make me something to eat?"

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:15.300
Like many other popular horror series, Castle
Rock is adopting an anthology format, albeit

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.380
one with storylines that might carry over
from season to season.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:23.220
In July 2018, co-showrunner Dustin Thomason
told The Hollywood Reporter:

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:28.180
"Each season is going to be its own self-contained
story: beginning, middle and end.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:31.620
But I think that just as the books do, we
want to surprise viewers with the ways in

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.020
which the stories intersect."

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:38.620
Aside from kitchen appliances coming to life,
taking over the world, and enslaving humanity,

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:42.710
you probably haven't thought much about how
the technology you depend on has the potential

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:45.080
to create your very own personal hellscape.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:50.400
Enter Black Mirror, a British import acquired
by Netflix, which aims to torture us with

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:50.900
tech.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:56.120
Created by Charlie Booker, Black Mirror tells
its tales in single-episode formats, kind

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.300
of like The Twilight Zone or The Outer Limits.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:02.360
Much like those shows, some are more disturbing
or frightening than others.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:06.690
Some are downright uplifting, such as "San
Junipero," starring Gugu Mbatha-Raw and Mackenzie

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:10.280
Davis as a young couple who find happiness
in a virtual afterlife.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:15.220
Some, on the other hand, are straight-up laugh-out-loud
hilarious, in a disturbing kind of way, of

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:15.720
course.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:20.160
Take, for example, the Bryce Dallas Howard-led
"Nosedive," which digs its claws into our

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:23.850
dangerous obsession with social media and
the dystopia it could inspire.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:26.620
"Come on, let's have a little fun here!

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:28.880
You know, f--- the planet!

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.520
You know f--- the planet!"

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:36.820
Still, the vast majority of the episodes are
downright terrifying, like the coincidentally

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:41.430
named "White Bear" and "White Christmas,"
which both present a criminal justice system

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:45.900
in which perpetrators are imprisoned and tortured
inside realities that aren't exactly what

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:46.480
they seem.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:51.780
AMC's The Terror has been described as a horror
thriller disguised as a period drama.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:57.370
The inaugural season was based on Dan Simmons'
2007 bestselling novel of the same name and

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:02.900
stars Mad Men's Jared Harris as Captain Francis
Crozier, whose 19th century Arctic exploration

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:03.600
turns deadly.

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:09.490
When the Arctic freezes and two giant seafaring
ships are trapped in ice, a mysterious menace

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:11.820
begins killing off the sailors one by one.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:17.500
But it's not clear if the menace is supernatural,
human, or if the sailors are simply going

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:18.000
mad.

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:21.940
What's more frightening than not knowing if
the horrible things happening around you are

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:22.440
real?

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:28.360
In June 2018, Variety reported that The Terror
had been renewed for a second season, which

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:32.890
will reportedly be set on the west coast of
the U.S. during World War II and focus on

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:34.660
a Japanese-American community.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:39.540
Star Trek's George Takei is set to appear
as a series regular, portraying a former fishing

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:41.720
captain and an elder figure in his community.

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:46.320
Collider reports that Takei, who spent part
of his childhood in a Japanese internment

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:51.000
camp, will also be acting as a consultant
to ensure "the accuracy of historical events

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.000
and storytelling."

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:58.220
Based on the novel of the same name by Gillian
Flynn, HBO's Sharp Objects stars Amy Adams

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:00.080
as crime reporter Camille Parker.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:05.000
After struggling for years with alcoholism
and self-harm, Camille returns to her hometown

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:07.710
to report on the murders of two young girls.

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:11.020
Patricia Clarkson plays Camille's cold and
distant mother.

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:13.580
"When you're here, you're my daughter.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:17.420
You can move away and forget, but I can't.

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:19.490
You don't know the people here anymore."

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:24.120
In addition to telling a gripping story, Sharp
Objects acts as a study in depression.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:28.200
Camille's flashbacks are blurry, disjointed,
and untrustworthy.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:32.370
Her self-harm is heartbreaking, and her line
of work only contributes to her inability

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:35.480
to dig out of a hole that keeps her trapped
in her own troubled mind.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:39.980
What makes Sharp Objects all the more tragic
is how very real it can be.

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:45.690
Unlike shows that deal with supernatural elements,
Camille's story is one grounded in reality,

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:47.660
and experienced by real people every day.

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:52.460
Her isolation and fractured family life make
for a difficult watch for anyone with a troubled

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:52.960
past.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:57.280
Camille might be alone, but make sure you're
not without a friendly hand to squeeze when

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:58.880
when the tension gets a little too high.

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:04.760
It might seem odd that Ryan Murphy, the creator
of the happy musical high school dramedy Glee,

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:09.210
could also be responsible for FX's American
Horror Story, one of the most frightening

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:10.160
shows on television.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:15.550
American Horror Story's anthology framework
allows for a different setting every season.

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:19.340
Some are scarier than others, some even flirt
with the horror comedy genre.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:22.200
"B------ want pâté?

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:24.280
Pâté they shall have."

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:25.820
But all of them have their moments.

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:28.420
It all depends on what really makes you jump.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:33.730
Whether it's witches, scary clowns, haunted
houses, or even politics, there's probably

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:38.080
an American Horror Story season that is tailor
made to set off your worst nightmares.

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:43.530
And the repertory casting puts actors like
Sarah Paulson, Evan Peters, Kathy Bates, Taissa

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:48.320
Farmiga, and Jessica Lange, among many others
in different roles every season, which allows

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:50.710
them to stretch their creepiest acting muscles.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:55.300
If anything, it provides audiences with the
comfort of some familiar faces throughout

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:57.340
all of that unfamiliar darkness.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:03.040
Let's get one thing straight: While this Netflix
series and its early '90s sitcom counterpart

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:08.419
both take inspiration from the pages of Archie
Comics' Sabrina the Teenage Witch, this adaptation

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.140
definitely embraces the "chilling" part of
its title.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:16.440
Starring Mad Men's Kiernan Shipka, The Chilling
Adventures of Sabrina focuses on the 16-year-old

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:20.360
title character, who must reconcile her status
as half-witch, half-human.

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:23.660
"'Brina, we want…we need to ask you"

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:24.680
"Are you a witch?"

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:25.180
("Are you a witch?")

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:33.020
In addition to trying to decide between pledging
allegiance to the Dark Lord Satan and hanging

00:08:33.029 --> 00:08:37.459
out with her very human boyfriend, Sabrina
also battles literal demons that threaten

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:39.120
the way of life she's always known.

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:43.880
What's really scary for one person might be
totally fine for someone else, but Sabrina

00:08:43.889 --> 00:08:48.220
definitely has a creep factor that will make
you wish you weren't alone, particularly when

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:49.840
it comes to the whole Satan thing.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:53.380
That's one creepy take on everybody's favorite
fallen angel.

